\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Supply-temperature flexibility. Lowering the plant supply temperature reduces thermal loss but shrinks the temperature difference, so flow and pumping rise. The cost-optimal reduction is 17.5\,K; beyond 20\,K the pipe velocity limit binds, and hydraulics change from a negligible cost into the binding constraint.}}{27}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tsup}{{8}{27}{Supply-temperature flexibility. Lowering the plant supply temperature reduces thermal loss but shrinks the temperature difference, so flow and pumping rise. The cost-optimal reduction is 17.5\,K; beyond 20\,K the pipe velocity limit binds, and hydraulics change from a negligible cost into the binding constraint}{figure.8}{}}
